# Constructor arguments the .pyi marks omittable that the binding requires, and
# that doppler cannot fix on its own. Both faces are jm-generated, so there is
# no local change that makes them agree — only the upstream one. Each entry is
# `Class.param`, and check_init_param_optionality.py reports an entry that has
# stopped diverging, so this list cannot quietly outlive its reason.
#
# NOT a jm bug, and NOT upstream-blocked: doppler's own stale sacred fragment.
# `acquire_ext_carrier_acq.c` was written when psd_template came first and had
# no default. The manifest later moved it and gave it `default = "[]"`, the
# .pyi followed, and a sacred fragment's constructor is never rewritten -- so
# the stub advertises `psd_template=` as omittable over a binding that still
# demands it first. jm reports this on every `jm apply`, by name, as
# kwargs-drift; it is a warning in a list of warnings, which is exactly how it
# survived (see just-makeit#823, where the ask is to GATE what is already
# detected).
#
# Deleting the fragment and re-applying fixes it outright and loses no members
# -- verified. It is parked rather than done because it changes the
# constructor's POSITIONAL order (psd_template stops being argument 1), and
# doppler's own tests and examples call it positionally in the old order. That
# is a public API break either way round, so it needs its own change:
#
#   (a) regenerate + update the call sites -- honest, breaks positional callers
#   (b) reconcile the MANIFEST to the shipped binding (psd_template first, no
#       default) -- non-breaking, and arguably truer: every caller already
#       passes it, spelling "not supplied" as an empty array
#
# Recommend (b). Delete this line with whichever lands.
CarrierAcquisition.psd_template

# just-makeit#823 Ask C, a different mechanism reaching the same symptom. A
# capsule init-param (gh-790) rejects Py_None unconditionally, so its binding
# has no `|` at all, while the stub still renders it `= ...`. A capsule METHOD
# param (gh-432) already maps None -> NULL, so the two capsule paths disagree.
#
# The C means something by NULL here: "no time base stated", after which the
# capture's sidecar omits the keys rather than fabricating a sample rate into a
# file that outlives the process. Python cannot say it yet. The docstrings say
# so plainly rather than promising a None that raises.
#
# Remove BOTH when the pin carries Ask C; no signature changes, the TypeError
# simply becomes a working call.
MemoryCapture.clock
Capture.clock
